From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Skin Fixer Tooling <tooling@skinfixer.local>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 08:08:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: workspace scene builder, remove SampleScene

Adds a generated workspace scene for reviewing skin deformation, and clears the
URP template's SampleScene out of the project.

The scene is built by script rather than shipped as a hand written .unity file.
Unity writes YAML for the exact editor version in use, the scene can be rebuilt
at any time from Tools > Skin Weight Tools > Create Workspace Scene, and the
patch stays reviewable.

New:
- SkinFixerWorkspace (Runtime): scene marker holding the Models root, preview
  camera, three light rig and ground reference. Exposes TryGetModelBounds so the
  tooling can frame whatever is loaded regardless of model scale.
- WorkspaceSceneBuilder (Editor): builds and saves the scene to
  Assets/SkinWeightTools/Scenes/SkinFixer_Workspace.unity. Neutral grey
  background and flat ambient so shading reads honestly, key/fill/rim
  directional lights with shadows on the key only, and a ground plane with its
  collider stripped. URP companion components are attached by reflected type
  name, so the tool still compiles in a Built-in or HDRP project.

Changed:
- SkinnedMeshImportUtility parents imports under the workspace Models root and
  frames them on arrival, when a workspace is present in the scene.
- SkinWeightToolsWindow gains a Workspace section on the Source tab: create the
  scene, frame the model, toggle the ground plane.

Removed:
- Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity and its meta, plus the now empty Scenes folder.
- The SampleScene entry in EditorBuildSettings, leaving m_Scenes empty.
